{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Behold, the children of Israel have not listened to me</b> — for You have not made my words heard to them. <b>And how shall Pharaoh listen to me?</b> — and furthermore, for <b>I am of uncircumcised lips</b> and I am not fit to speak before a great king. And it is possible to explain that Moses thought perhaps it was because of his own unworthiness that they did not listen to him, for he is of uncircumcised lips and cannot prepare to speak to their heart good words, words of comfort — how much more so to speak to Pharaoh. And the reason for this verse is that at first He did not command him to speak himself to Pharaoh, but only said, \"And you shall come, you and the elders of Israel, to the king of Egypt, and you shall say to him\" (Exodus 3:18), and it was possible that the elders would speak and he would be silent. And he was ashamed to speak even to the people, and he said, \"I am not a man of words\" (Exodus 4:10). And HaKadosh Baruch Hu answered him, \"And he shall speak for you to the people\" (ibid. v. 16), and so it was when they first came, as it says (ibid. v. 30), \"And Aaron spoke all the words which YHWH had spoken to Moses, and he did the signs before the eyes of the people.\" And now, when Moses was commanded, \"Therefore say to the children of Israel: I am YHWH,\" he himself spoke to them as he was commanded, and they did not listen to him. And when He again commanded him to speak to Pharaoh, he said: How shall I speak to him, <b>and I am of uncircumcised lips?</b> And HaKadosh Baruch Hu joined Aaron with him and commanded both of them to the children of Israel, that they should speak to them all that He would command them, and to Pharaoh, to bring them out of his land. And Rashi explained (Rashi on Exodus 6:13) concerning the matter of the children of Israel and concerning his mission to Pharaoh. And there is no need."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:03:50.416867779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}